    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that rejects owner creation when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, responding with **409 Conflict**.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`CityAtCapacityException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` following the existing `DuplicateHouseholdException`/`DuplicateTelephoneException` pattern in the `rest.advice` package.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after required-field validation (so a well-formed payload is what's being counted), it counts existing owners whose city matches case-insensitively (reusing the same `equalsIgnoreCase` comparison already used by `nextCustomerCode`) and throws `CityAtCapacityException` when the count is `>= 50`. Added the corresponding import.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `CityAtCapacityException` that returns `409 CONFLICT` with `{\"errors\": [\"city\"]}`, matching the shape of the sibling 409 handlers.\n\n**Test result:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fill a fresh city to exactly 50, then expect the 51st to be rejected as 409) passes.",
